{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 2,
  "is_atomic": false,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When a marshaling station is \"used\" (i.e., any positive quantity is transshipped through it), is the fixed cost f_k incurred exactly once regardless of how much flows through it?",
    "Is the goal to minimize the sum of these fixed costs plus all unit transportation costs?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains two semantically independent questions: one clarifying the nature of the fixed cost (whether it is a one-time charge per station) and another clarifying the objective function (whether it minimizes the sum of fixed and variable costs). A user could confirm the cost structure without confirming the objective, or vice versa."
}

